nd we  are never going to see that for one very  simple reason there is no way in heck  Warner Brothers would ever be able to  recoup the expenses of finishing it  because post-production special effects  are dang expensive now they could  release whatever they currently have  which as I said most likely is a work  print a rough cut and they could release  it as it is with placeholders and  unfinished special effects and that will  cost them virtually nothing to do but  the thing is and I think Warner Brothers  knows this that won't satisfy the people  calling from the Snyder cut they will  simply then start shouting you gave us  an incomplete movie you didn't give the  film a chance to be seen properly the  way it was meant to be seen but again  like that would like minimum minimum for  just using Justice League as a template  for how high a percentage of the film is  going to be special effects for my money  minimum hundred million dollars to get  the Snyder cut even vaguely up to a  releasable standard in terms of what  would have been expected to hit theaters  at the time the Justice League movie  came out and whatever others is never  going to spend that because as loud as  the Snyder cut people are and as much as  to my frustration and annoyance it keeps  getting refreshed because the reason  this came up is gal gadot and Ben  Affleck both tweeted out hashtag  released the Snyder cut why did they get  on this bandwagon I have no idea but it  keeps getting refreshed but what these  people want is not  realistic and I'm not and again I'm not  even saying I wouldn't like to see that  I would said that early on it and I  stand by that but no studio is going to  shell out again  ballpark had a guess somebody uneducated  but I still feel confident in this  number about a hundred million dollars  for a niche alternate cut that you know  to just to placate a relatively small  audience especially when the franchise  as a whole is doing just fine in the  absence of the 